From eb2067033c0414553246350c2166724cf1fc7385 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anatoliy Klymenko <anatoliy.klymenko@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Aug 2025 17:13:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 049/190] drm: xlnx: vtc: Configure pixel clock

commit 40e9eecb81435646ac981e94f9c33a3202d60afb from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

Configuring PL display output pipeline requires video timing to be set in
accordance with the selected display mode. VTC driver performs this task.
Except for tuning the pixel clock. This clock may be configured separately
in the participating CRTC driver. Although, for now, we have multiple PL
IP/CRTC combos, while video timing is being handled by VTC exclusively. So,
the VTC driver is the perfect place to set the pixel clock covering all PL
CRTCs at once.

Signed-off-by: Anatoliy Klymenko <anatoliy.klymenko@amd.com>
Reviewed-by: Vishal Sagar <vishal.sagar@amd.com>
Message-ID: <20250821001303.1178351-7-anatoliy.klymenko@amd.com>
State: pending
Signed-off-by: Quanyang Wang <quanyang.wang@windriver.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_vtc.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_vtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_vtc.c
index 804a951f666c..a30a6d307efa 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_vtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_vtc.c
@@ -198,10 +198,15 @@ static int xlnx_vtc_set_timing(struct xlnx_bridge *bridge,
 	u32 htotal, hactive, hsync_start, hbackporch_start;
 	u32 vtotal, vactive, vsync_start, vbackporch_start;
 	struct xlnx_vtc *vtc = bridge_to_vtc(bridge);
+	int ret;
 
 	reg = xlnx_vtc_readl(vtc->base, XVTC_CTL);
 	xlnx_vtc_writel(vtc->base, XVTC_CTL, reg & ~XVTC_CTL_RU);
 
+	ret = clk_set_rate(vtc->vid_clk, vm->pixelclock / vtc->ppc);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		dev_err(vtc->dev, "failed to set pixel clock rate: %d\n", ret);
+
 	vm->hactive /= vtc->htiming_div_fact;
 	vm->hfront_porch /= vtc->htiming_div_fact;
 	vm->hback_porch /= vtc->htiming_div_fact;
